Changed: A parallel::shared::Triangulation with artificial cells now packs
data attached to cells (e.g., by SolutionTransfer) on locally owned cells
only and sends it to the new owners after mesh refinement. This is what
parallel::distributed::Triangulation already does, and it fixes the
transfer of data if cells change their owner. As a consequence,
SolutionTransfer now requires distributed vectors with ghost entries on such
triangulations. In addition, the METIS and Zoltan partitioners now assign
all children of a cell to the same owner if they are all active, so that
they can be coarsened on one process. A user defined partition
(partition_custom_signal) has to do this itself.
<br>
(Matthias Maier, 2026/11/27)
